      "start_seconds": 1.27,
      "end_seconds": 5.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Hi, doctor, I hope I'm not disturbing you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.83,
      "end_seconds": 11.87,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "not at all, please sit what seems to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 13.28,
      "end_seconds": 20.17,
      "duration_seconds": 6.89,
      "text": "Let me think, morning, doctor. I'll stay and fill in anything that's missed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.55,
      "end_seconds": 27.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "Yes, that's no problem at all. Please sit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 32.26,
      "end_seconds": 36.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.68,
      "text": "So, we came because of a mole that is itching."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.5,
      "end_seconds": 40.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.28,
      "end_seconds": 51.26,
      "duration_seconds": 6.98,
      "text": "A crusty edge on the mole goes along with it, most of the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.71,
      "end_seconds": 57.71,
      "duration_seconds": 5.0,
      "text": "what about bleeding from the mole once, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.03,
      "end_seconds": 66.4,
      "duration_seconds": 7.37,
      "text": "Yes, I have. The crusty edge on the mole? That's been for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.81,
      "end_seconds": 70.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Time for your numbers, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.79,
      "end_seconds": 86.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.15,
      "end_seconds": 108.34,
      "duration_seconds": 9.19,
      "text": "Okay: blood pressure 119 over 71, temp 36.6 degrees, oxygen saturation is 99 percent. And pulse 84, respiratory rate 14."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.66,
      "end_seconds": 114.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.52,
      "end_seconds": 117.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.19,
      "text": "Look straight ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.07,
      "end_seconds": 143.93,
      "duration_seconds": 8.86,
      "text": "there is a dark, six-millimetre mole with an irregular border and two shades of brown on the upper back"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.11,
      "end_seconds": 146.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.19,
      "text": "breathe out slowly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.74,
      "end_seconds": 158.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "I can't feel any glands in the armpit or neck"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.63,
      "end_seconds": 167.93,
      "duration_seconds": 7.3,
      "text": "so, all finished, thank you let me check a few things any pain or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.56,
      "end_seconds": 171.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "Nope, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.38,
      "end_seconds": 177.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.14,
      "text": "did you get family history of melanoma or other new moles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.61,
      "end_seconds": 180.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "none of those, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.73,
      "end_seconds": 186.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.6,
      "text": "Alright, any pins and needles or loss of strength anywhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.34,
      "end_seconds": 191.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Oh, no, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.56,
      "end_seconds": 195.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "What operations have you had, if any?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.72,
      "end_seconds": 209.92,
      "duration_seconds": 13.2,
      "text": "yes, I had a wisdom tooth extraction under sedation, five years ago i'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.27,
      "end_seconds": 212.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "and your job?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.18,
      "end_seconds": 217.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "I work in accounts at a hospital."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.35,
      "end_seconds": 221.06,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "Who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.95,
      "end_seconds": 224.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "My partner and our baby"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.82,
      "end_seconds": 247.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 247.67,
      "end_seconds": 256.99,
      "duration_seconds": 9.32,
      "text": "okay, so he is on omeprazole, 20 milligrams, once a day for the reflux, I give it to him"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.05,
      "end_seconds": 262.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "how long has that been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 263.66,
      "end_seconds": 265.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "About a year now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.36,
      "end_seconds": 277.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 278.73,
      "end_seconds": 286.2,
      "duration_seconds": 7.47,
      "text": "Acid reflux, for nearly five years. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.8,
      "end_seconds": 296.34,
      "duration_seconds": 8.54,
      "text": "putting it all together, it points towards a a pigmented lesion that needs removal for a proper diagnosis"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 299.46,
      "end_seconds": 300.91,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.48,
      "end_seconds": 336.87,
      "duration_seconds": 35.39,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now a pigmented lesion that needs removal for a proper diagnosis is my leading thought, not anything worse. I want a skin biopsy done, that's for changing mole. I want a dermoscopy done, that's for changing mole. Cover up and use factor 50 sunscreen on exposed skin. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day. I'll also refer you to the skin cancer clinic."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 342.14,
      "end_seconds": 351.14,
      "duration_seconds": 9.0,
      "text": "the thing that would worry me is if the mole bleeds or grows quickly if that happens, go to emergency"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 352.88,
      "end_seconds": 357.07,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Oh, okay, I'll look out for that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 358.07,
      "end_seconds": 364.8,
      "duration_seconds": 6.73,
      "text": "We'll catch up after the biopsy results. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 366.21,
      "end_seconds": 370.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "No, uh, that's all. Thanks a lot."
    }
  ]
